## The State of Recalls: Class II Domination  
2026 has seen a significant number of food recalls, with 433 incidents reported so far. This includes 105 Class I recalls, the most severe category, and a staggering 293 Class II recalls, mainly involving undeclared allergens and foreign objects. This trend of mid-level hazards raises questions about quality control.  
## Highlighted Incidents  
May 2026 saw its share of recalls, including multiple incidents involving the Dakota Honey Company due to foreign objects such as stainless steel dust and plastic flakes found in their honey products. Consumers need to remain cautious and informed.  
## Repeat Offenders: A Cause for Concern  
Brands like Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC continue to disappoint, each with 11 recalls this year, mostly Class I. These repeat offenders undermine trust and highlight systemic issues in food safety compliance.
